==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|λεξικός||of words}}, from {{m|grc|λέξις||a saying, speech, word}}, from {{m|grc|λέγειν||to speak}} + [[-logy]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|lexicologies}}

# {{label|en|uncountable|linguistics}} The part of [[linguistics]] that studies [[word]]s, their nature and meaning, words' elements, relations between words including [[semantic]] relations, words groups and the whole [[lexicon]].
#* '''1949''' ''Journal of Theological Studies''
#*: The fifth is devoted to doctrine; the sixth and seventh to remarks on syntax and '''lexicology''' respectively.
# {{label|en|countable}} A specific theory concerning the lexicon.

